 "rules": [
  "Scored on the held-out half of the frozen sample only (TOIs by sha256(seed:TIC) parity); the tuning half is never scored.",
  "A submission covers every star of its scope: the whole held-out half, or the Sentinels' stated 40-star subsample. A star without a light curve is submitted with searched: false and counts as missed in the all-stars completeness, which is the rank key.",
  "It states the sha256 of the public inputs it was built from (tuning half with labels, held-out half without). Any other hash, tuned_on other than none or tuning, a label field in a prediction, a missing or extra star, or missing provenance: refused, with the reasons listed.",
  "The hash is an attestation: the held-out labels are public in the repository, so the leaderboard cannot prove they were not read. It refuses every submission that declares or shows that they were.",
  "Completeness: CP/KP stars whose TOI dip the method recovered (passed its vetting). FP rejection: searched FP stars whose TOI dip the method did not offer as a clean candidate (recovered and not flagged). Controls: stars with any vetted event on the flux-inverted and block-scrambled light curves. Reliability: the share of clean candidates on TOI dips that are CP/KP, on this sample's class mix, which is not the TOI catalogue's.",
  "All rates carry Wilson 95% intervals. TFOPWG dispositions are the reference, not ground truth for every TOI.",
  "Measured on a stated benchmark; nothing on this leaderboard is a discovery."
 ],
